data science has become a big buzzword  in the business world today companies  have been actively hiring data  scientists Python developers and machine  learning engineers to build data science  teams in order to capitalize on the vast  volumes of data that these companies  generate daily business managers realize  that there's value in the data that they  have access to often though they are  just not sure how to extract it and  achieve meaningful business impact and  this is confirmed by a recent Garten  study which reported that 85% of all  data science projects fail to understand  why this is the case let's look at the  results of a survey run by cago last  year the survey had a question on the  biggest challenges that businesses faced  in their data science efforts the survey  identified 15 most common data science  challenges these 15 challenges can be  grouped into four distinct categories  the first category deals with data  almost half of the respondents reported  the impure data as the ultimate top  challenge also we learn that obtaining  data for the data science projects might  be hard  besides privacy issues post specific  challenges to you'll probably come as no  surprise to anyone familiar with data  science projects to see data related  issues as the major hurdle the second  category of challenges is related to  human factor over 40% of the survey  participants feel that there's a  shortage of the qualified data science  engineers in the field besides it is  evident that communication and  collaboration is another major issue  implementing data science projects  usually involves three main stakeholders  business IT and of course data science  this survey shows there are clear issues  of collaboration and communication  between these camps lack of managerial  support lack of clear questions to  address results are not used or  implemented by the business difficulty  deploying and coordinating with IT and  difficulty explaining data science the  third category of challenges identified  by the survey was related to limitations  of available tools most data science  tools reach their limits relatively  quickly  which forces machine learning engineers  to create custom developed code in order  to optimize the computing time required  to run the models the fourth category of  challenges was linked to lack of  financial support of the data science  projects almost 40 percent of the  respondents answered that the lack of  financial support hinders their data  science efforts this becomes a major  issue especially when the data science  projects grow big and the size of the  data you're using in the projects is  usually positively correlated with the  cost the bigger the data the more  difficult it is to control the costs as  a result the companies need to employ  more expensive technology stack more  expensive talent and more computing  power  in order to improve the odds of  achieving a positive ROI of a data  science project businesses need to be  aware of these challenges and find means  of addressing them effectively
 

